# The files the NSIS bundler of tauri-bundler 2.10 (the one inside
# @tauri-apps/cli 2.12.3, see package-lock.json) looks for in
# ~/.cache/tauri/NSIS on a Linux host, and downloads when they are not
# there. The recipe puts them there first, checked against the sha256
# below, so the bundler downloads nothing. Check them again at every bump
# of the Tauri CLI: NSIS_TAURI_UTILS_URL, NSIS_URL and NSIS_EXE_SHA1 in
# crates/tauri-bundler/src/bundle/windows/nsis/mod.rs.
#
# nsis_tauri_utils.dll: a plugin the installer template calls, packed
# into every installer and run on the user's machine at install time.
# The bundler checks it against a SHA-1 of its own
# (75197fee3c6a814fe035788d1c34ead39349b860).
#   https://github.com/tauri-apps/nsis-tauri-utils/releases/download/nsis_tauri_utils-v0.5.3/nsis_tauri_utils.dll
#
# NSIS.exe: never run and never shipped. makensis comes from the pinned
# nsis package of the image. Since tauri-cli 2.12.3 (tauri-apps/tauri
# #16237) the bundler checks NSIS.exe against a SHA-1 on every host,
# Linux included, where it never was, then deletes the NSIS directory and
# downloads the plugin again: the offline build fails on it. The recipe
# takes NSIS.exe out of the NSIS 3.13 archive the bundler names, whose
# SHA-1 the bundler also pins (db14f8af2ea346b786c6ae19343f61aaf5e09b8e;
# GitHub digest of asset 623832696, uploaded 2026-10-09, the same sha256
# as below), and the bundler finds the SHA-1 it wants
# (6d45d4e8ccf18fe1fdac9164058f356102a2ecf2).
#   https://github.com/tauri-apps/binary-releases/releases/download/nsis-3.13/nsis-3.13.zip
5ba143b5db4a87d32d6e7802e033330aae56cbceabe0d1e3ba41948385ad4709  nsis_tauri_utils.dll
ba63dffc4410ee89193e1cb5a41989991bd77c61068da17e3156d136b7b0b3d8  nsis-3.13.zip
78e17de55fa013be7620487e85b6676c204c6c51d7ebabb74ee8a9cfce6252a0  NSIS.exe
